      en: "The Main Guard House, built in 1803 in Bridgetown, served as the headquarters for the British garrison's guard. Located at National Heroes Square opposite the Parliament, this two-story neoclassical building now houses the Barbados Museum & Historical Society. Its facade features a columned portico and a wrought-iron balcony. Originally, soldiers stationed here maintained public order. The museum's exhibits include military uniforms, weapons, and colonial artifacts. The building is part of the UNESCO World Heritage site 'Historic Bridgetown and its Garrison'.",
