      en: "The Da Costa Building, constructed in 1905 on Broad Street in Bridgetown, was designed for the import-export firm Da Costa & Co. in the Belle Époque style. Its facade features elaborate terracotta detailing and a mansard roof with dormer windows. Originally a department store, it later housed offices. The building is a rare survival of French-inspired architecture in Barbados. After a 1980s renovation, it now contains retail spaces on the ground floor and offices above. It is listed on the Barbados National Building Registry.",
